ills/gws-sheets-read resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-sheets-read\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-slides resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-slides\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-tasks resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-tasks\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-email-to-task resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-email-to-task\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-file-announce resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-file-announce\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-meeting-prep resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-meeting-prep\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-standup-report resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-standup-report\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-weekly-digest resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-weekly-digest\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=agents-skills-personal root=~/.agents/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.agents/skills/weather/SKILL.md resolved=~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/weather/SKILL.md\nOpenClaw security audit\nSummary: 6 critical · 5 warn · 1 info\nRun deeper: openclaw security audit --deep\n\nCRITICAL\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated Open groupPolicy with elevated tools enabled\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy\nWith tools.elevated enabled, a prompt injection in those rooms can become a high-impact incident.\n  Fix: Set groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" and keep elevated allowlists extremely tight.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs Open groupPolicy with runtime/filesystem tools exposed\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy\nRisky tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nPrompt injection in open groups can trigger command/file actions in these contexts.\n  Fix: For open groups, prefer tools.profile=\"messaging\" (or deny group:runtime/group:fs), set tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, and use agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\" for exposed agents.\nplugins.code_safety Plugin \"claude-mem\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 6 critical issue(s) in 10 scanned file(s):\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/bun-runner.js:51)\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6)\n  - [dynamic-code-execution] Dynamic code execution detected (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:57)\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/smart-install.js:78)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (plugin/scripts/worker-cli.js:5)\n  Fix: Review the plugin source code carefully before use. If untrusted, remove the plugin from your OpenClaw extensions state directory.\nskills.code_safety Skill \"tavily\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 2 critical issue(s) in 2 scanned file(s) under /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/tavily-search:\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (scripts/extract.mjs:25)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (scripts/search.mjs:49)\n  Fix: Review the skill source code before use. If untrusted, remove \"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/tavily-search\".\nskills.code_safety Skill \"writing-skills\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 1 critical issue(s) in 1 scanned file(s) under /home/lfant/.agents/skills/writing-skills:\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (render-graphs.js:25)\n  Fix: Review the skill source code before use. If untrusted, remove \"/home/lfant/.agents/skills/writing-skills\".\nchannels.telegram.warning.1 Telegram security warning\n  Telegram groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" with no channels.telegram.groups allowlist; any group can add + ping (mention-gated). Set channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom or configure channels.telegram.groups.\n\nWARN\ngateway.trusted_proxies_missing Reverse proxy headers are not trusted\n  gateway.bind is loopback and gateway.trustedProxies is empty. If you expose the Control UI through a reverse proxy, configure trusted proxies so local-client checks cannot be spoofed.\n  Fix: Set gateway.trustedProxies to your proxy IPs or keep the Control UI local-only.\ntools.exec.auto_allow_skills_enabled autoAllowSkills is enabled for exec approvals\n  Implicit skill-bin allowlisting is enabled at:\n- defaults.autoAllowSkills\nThis widens host exec trust beyond explicit manual allowlist entries.\n  Fix: Disable autoAllowSkills in exec approvals and keep manual allowlists tight when you need explicit host-exec trust.\nsecurity.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic Potential multi-user setup detected (personal-assistant model warning)\n  Heuristic signals indicate this gateway may be reachable by multiple users:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"\nRuntime/process tools are exposed without full sandboxing in at least one context.\nPotential high-impact tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nOpenClaw's default security model is personal-assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant isolation on one shared gateway.\n  Fix: If users may be mutually untrusted, split trust boundaries (separate gateways + credentials, ideally separate OS users/hosts). If you intentionally run shared-user access, set agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\", keep tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, deny runtime/fs/web tools unless required, and keep personal/private identities + credentials off that runtime.\nplugins.allow_phantom_entries plugins.allow contains entries with no matching installed plugin\n  The following plugins.allow entries do not correspond to any installed plugin: telegram, memory-core, zai, openai, openrouter.\nPhantom entries could be exploited by registering a new plugin with an allowlisted ID.\n  Fix: Remove unused entries from plugins.allow, or verify the expected plugins are installed.\nplugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n  Enabled extension plugins: claude-mem.\nPermissive tool policy contexts:\n- default\n- agents.list.main\n  Fix: Use restrictive profiles (`minimal`/`coding`) or explicit tool allowlists that exclude plugin tools for agents handling untrusted input.\n\nINFO\nsummary.attack_surface Attack surface summary\n  groups: open=1, allowlist=0\ntools.elevated: enabled\nhooks.webhooks: disabled\nhooks.internal: enabled\nbrowser control: enabled\ntrust model: personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant on one shared gateway\n[agents/auth-profiles] synced openai-codex credentials from external cli\n","name":"openclaw security"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776535230669}}
{"type":"message","id":"31b10483","parentId":"352e0e6c","timestamp":"2026-04-18T18:01:02.189Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"보안 감사가 완료되었습니다. 이제 결과를 분석하고 사용자가 요청한 오탐(false positives)을 필터링하여 보고해야 합니다.\n\n사용자가 무시하라고 지정한 오탐:\n1. tavily-search: scripts/extract.mjs, scripts/search.mjs\n2. claude-mem: bun-runner.js, context-generator.cjs, mcp-server.cjs, smart-install.js, worker-cli.js\n3. writing-skills: render-graphs.js\n\n요약 결과 (필터링 후):\n- Critical: 6개\n- Warn: 5개  \n- Info: 1개\n\n오탐 제거:\n- plugins.code_safety - \"claude-mem\" (6개) → 전부 제거\n- skills.code_safety - \"tavily\" (2개) → 전부 제거\n- skills.code_safety - \"writing-skills\" (1개) → 전부 제거\n\n실제 Critical 이슈 (오탐 제거 후):\n1. security.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated\n2. security.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs\n3. channels.telegram.warning.1 (Warn이지만 주목해야 함)\n\nWarn 이슈:\n1. gateway.trusted_proxies_missing\n2. tools.exec.auto_allow_skills_enabled\n3. security.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic\n4. plugins.allow_phantom_entries\n5. plugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy\n\nInfo:\n1. summary.attack_surface\n\n이제 한국어로 보고를 작성하겠습니다.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## 📋 일일 보안 감사 보고서\n\n**실행 시각**: 2026-04-19 03:00 (KST)  \n**명령어**: `openclaw security audit --deep`  \n**요약**: 6 Critical · 5 Warn · 1 Info\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ CRITICAL (6건)\n\n#### 1. security.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated\nElevated tools이 활성화된 상태에서 open groupPolicy가 설정됨\n\n**위치**: `channels.telegram.groupPolicy = \"open\"`\n\n**위험**: 오픈 그룹에서 프롬프트 인젝션 발생 시 고영향 인시던트로 확장 가능\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- groupPolicy를 `\"allowlist\"`로 설정\n- elevated allowlist를 극도로 제한적으로 유지\n\n---\n\n#### 2. security.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs\nRuntime/filesystem tools이 노출된 상태에서 open groupPolicy가 설정됨\n\n**위치**: `channels.telegram.groupPolicy = \"open\"`\n\n**위험한 tool exposure 컨텍스트**:\n- `agents.defaults` (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- `agents.list.main` (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- 오픈 그룹에서는 `tools.profile=\"messaging\"` 선호\n- `tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true` 설정\n- 노출된 에이전트에 `agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\"` 사용\n\n---\n\n#### 3. channels.telegram.warning.1\nTelegram 보안 경고\n\n**내용**: \n- Telegram groups: `groupPolicy=\"open\"` 설정 상태\n- `channels.telegram.groups` allowlist 미구성\n- 모든 그룹에서 추가 및 멘션(mention-gated) 가능\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- `channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` + `channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom` 설정\n- 또는 `channels.telegram.groups` 명시적 구성\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ WARN (5건)\n\n#### 1. gateway.trusted_proxies_missing\n리버스 프록시 헤더가 신뢰되지 않음\n\n**내용**: `gateway.bind`는 loopback이고 `gateway.trustedProxies`가 비어있음\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- Control UI를 리버스 프록시 통해 노출 시, proxy IP를 `trustedProxies`에 설정\n- Control UI를 로컬 전용으로 유지\n\n---\n\n#### 2. tools.exec.auto_allow_skills_enabled\nexec approvals에서 autoAllowSkills가 활성화됨\n\n**위치**: `defaults.autoAllowSkills`\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- autoAllowSkills 비활성화\n- 명시적 host-exec 신뢰가 필요할 때는 manual allowlist 유지\n\n---\n\n#### 3. security.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic\n다중 사용자 환경 감지 (personal-assistant 모델 경고)\n\n**신호**:\n- `channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"`\n- Runtime/process tools이 적어도 하나의 컨텍스트에서 완전 샌드박싱 없이 노출됨\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- 사용자 간 상호 신뢰가 없는 경우: 별도 게이트웨이 + 자격증명, 별도 OS 사용자/호스트 분리\n- 공유 사용자 액세스 의도적인 경우:\n  - `agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\"` 설정\n  - `tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true` 유지\n  - 필요 시 runtime/fs/web tools 제한\n  - personal/private ID 및 자격증명을 해당 런타임에서 분리\n\n---\n\n#### 4. plugins.allow_phantom_entries\n`plugins.allow`에 설치되지 않은 플러그인 항목 존재\n\n**Phantom entries**: telegram, memory-core, zai, openai, openrouter\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- 사용하지 않는 `plugins.allow` 항목 제거\n- 또는 예상 플러그인이 설치되었는지 확인\n\n---\n\n#### 5. plugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy\n확장 플러그인 tools가 허용적인 tool 정책에서 접근 가능\n\n**활성화된 확장 플러그인**: claude-mem\n\n**허용적인 tool 정책 컨텍스트**:\n- default\n- `agents.list.main`\n\n**권장 조치**:\n- 제한적인 프로필(`minimal`/`coding`) 사용\n- 신뢰되지 않은 입력을 처리하는 에이전트에서 플러그인 tools를 제외하는 명시적 tool allowlist\n\n---\n\n### ℹ️ INFO (1건)\n\n#### 1. summary.attack_surface\n공격 표면 요약\n\n- groups: open=1, allowlist=0\n- tools.elevated: enabled\n- hooks.webhooks: disabled\n- hooks.internal: enabled\n- browser control: enabled\n- trust model: personal assistant (신뢰된 오퍼레이터 경계), 적대적 multi-tenant 아님\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 무시된 오탐 (False Positives)\n\n다음 경고는 사용자 지시에 따라 제외됨:\n\n1. **plugins.code_safety** - \"claude-mem\" 플러그인 (6개 이슈)\n   - bun-runner.js:51, mcp-server.cjs:6, smart-install.js:78, worker-cli.js:5\n\n2. **skills.code_safety** - \"tavily\" 스킬 (2개 이슈)\n   - scripts/extract.mjs:25, scripts/search.mjs:49\n\n3. **skills.code_safety** - \"writing-skills\" 스킬 (1개 이슈)\n   - render-graphs.js:25\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 우선순위 권장 조치\n\n1. **즉시**: `channels.telegram.groupPolicy`를 `\"allowlist\"`로 변경하고 명시적 그룹 구성\n2. **높음**: `agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\"` 활성화 및 `tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true` 설정\n3. **중간**: `plugins.allow` phantom entries 정리\n4. **낮음**: `trustedProxies` 및 `autoAllowSkills` 설정 검토"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":3927,"output":2162,"cacheRead":15345,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21434,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776535230675,"responseId":"20260419020033b4f6f646755b47ea"}}
